        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ui): keep mount recovery retrying after stalled probes",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users waiting for the Control UI to recover after a failed app startup would stop receiving automatic retries when the cache-busted document probe stalled.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nEach recovery probe now uses an `AbortController` deadline tied to the existing mount timeout. An abort follows the same failure path as other network errors, so `recoveryInFlight` resets and the existing bounded retry schedule continues.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThe static Control UI fallback can recover from a stalled document request instead of requiring a manual page reload. Visible fallback content and the six-attempt limit are unchanged.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Added an isolated-window regression that leaves fetch pending until its signal aborts, then proves all six bounded recovery attempts can proceed.\n- Updated the existing probe assertion to require a cross-realm `AbortSignal`.\n- `git diff --check` passed.\n- `oxfmt --check ui/index.html ui/src/app/mount-fallback.test.ts` passed.\n- `git range-diff` after rebasing onto `3e4b3b370f944f3e22c5104cd7d78c955fef8b2d` showed an identical patch.\n- Claude Sonnet 4.6 autoreview: patch correct (0.92), no accepted or actionable findings.\n- [Secretless fork CI run 29401051732](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29401051732) passed (63 checks passed, 25 skipped, no failures).\n- No screenshot: this changes recovery timing/state only; the rendered fallback is unchanged.\n- AI-assisted: implemented with Codex. I inspected and understand the recovery state machine and tests.\n",
